+Standard checked-in live canary bundles now keep both human and machine-readable summaries current. `live-canary-summary.md` is the operator-facing report, and `live-canary-summary.json` is generated from the same summary and coverage logic used by strict/release checks. Run-guide record commands include both `--summary-out` and `--summary-json-out`, so a live recapture cannot refresh the markdown summary while leaving the JSON proof packet stale. The selected `outputs/live-canary-safe-first` packet follows this contract too, but remains only a focused selected-case gate until the complete canary pack is run.
